  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research and Advocacy for addressing climate induced L&amp;Ds with practical and scalable solution</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project has been contextualized based on the scopes of research and advocacy activities of Christian Aid&#x2019;s ongoing/upcoming projects; included (i) Gender Transformative Climate Resilient Microfinance Project (ii) Integrating climate change and gender transformative approach to microfinance (ii) Protecting assets of most vulnerable families (around 25% borrowers) from extreme climate risk by strengthening/ mitigating risk activities and transferring risk to insurance companies (iii) Documentation of guidelines/ tools developed and sharing them (iv) Identifying lessons learnt and sharing with the stakeholders who will be able to take forward the initiative (vi) Preparing Baseline and advocacy issues for Responding to Climate Change and COVID-19 crisis in Bangabandhu Colony Project and (vii) Facilitating women-led organizations/groups to plan and implement locally led resilience practices putting women&#x2019;s and leadership at the center of locally-led resilience building practices through Participatory Actions on Resilience (PAR) by Women Led CSOs</narrative>
  </description>
